# Target C p6 e7 closure

Exact support and phase certificate. Among all 27,763 S7-orbits of eight-support multisets (multiplicity at most three), 27,712 touch at least 13 triangle blocks, 5,133 have at least seven individually eligible empty blocks, 20 admit a pairwise-compatible empty heptuple, and those give 48 heptuples. The committed bound z<=3 leaves 25 heptuples on 9 support orbits. Exhausting every phase gives 46,413 phase configurations and 145,071 phase/heptuple pairs. For U=sum E_b over the seven empty blocks, the exact mod-2 rank census is rank 6: 63, rank 7: 4,522, rank 8: 140,486. Thus rank_Q(U)>=rank_F2(U)>3 in every case, contradicting U<=P with rank(P)=3. Hence e=7 is empty. This closes the remaining p=6 branch when combined with the committed e<=6, e=8, e=9, and e>=10 closures.
